  "faqTitle": "FAQ",
  "faqSubtitle": "Short answers, no marketing.",
  "faqQ1": "Does the port actually work?",
  "faqA1": "It boots, VRShell runs and head tracking is live. The one blocker: the VR display still shows black because app-side tracking state arrives as zero. The status page keeps the current list.",
  "faqQ2": "Is it safe to flash?",
  "faqA2": "There is real risk. Only the system partition gets flashed - writing a bootloader image older than the anti-rollback fuse allows hard-bricks sdm845 permanently. Read the docs flashing guide first.",
  "faqQ3": "Which headset does it run on?",
  "faqA3": "The Pico Neo 2 (A7B10 / PICOA7B10). Both the Eye and non-Eye SKUs work; eye tracking is extra work on top.",
  "faqQ4": "Where do Pico's proprietary files come from?",
  "faqA4": "From your own device or its stock OTA. The overlay repo carries a manifest of every blob needed - path, size, sha256 prefix, purpose - and none of them are committed to source repos.",
  "faqQ5": "What is vrhome?",
  "faqA5": "Our own VR home environment. Stock VRShell needs the closed Pico compositor; vrhome is a NativeActivity that puts 2D apps on floating panels and still launches real VR apps fullscreen.",
  "faqQ6": "What is the license?",
  "faqA6": "Everything we wrote is AGPL-3.0. Dumped Pico and vendor binaries remain property of their owners and live in dump repos for research only.",

  "aboutTitle": "About",
  "aboutSubtitle": "One port, one headset, every step in the open.",
  "aboutWhatTitle": "What it is",
  "aboutWhatBody": "Neosalsa runs LineageOS 17.1 - Android 10 via a phh GSI - on the Pico Neo 2, a headset that shipped with Android 8.1 and a heavily proprietary VR stack.",
  "aboutHowTitle": "How it works",
  "aboutHowBody": "GSI plus overlay plus your own Pico stack. The vendor partition is never touched, so every compatibility problem - the vold deadlock, the missing sound card, the ABI breaks - gets fixed on the system side with init rules and shim libraries.",
  "aboutGroupTitle": "The group",
  "aboutGroupBody": "Forty-six repositories under neosalsa, one per component: the device tree, the shims, the research notes, the dump repos, the VR home and this site.",
